{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mat-8-1","title":"Matthew 8:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ cleanses the leper; 5 heals the centurion's servant, 14 Peter's mother in law, 16 and many other diseased; 18 shows how he is to be followed; 23 stills the tempest on the sea; 28 drives the devils out of two men possessed; 31 and suffers them to go into the swine.</p>\n<p>come. 5:1 great. 18; 4:25; 12:15; 15:30; 19:2; 20:29; Mr 3:7; Lu 5:15; 14:25-27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-2","title":"Matthew 8:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>behold. Mr 1:40-45; Lu 5:12 a leper. 10:8; 26:6; Le 13:44-46; Nu 5:2,3; 12:10; De 24:8,9; 2Sa 3:39 2Ki 5:1,27; 7:3,4; 15:5; 2Ch 26:19-21; Lu 4:27; 17:12-19 worshipped. 2:11; 4:9; 14:33; 15:25; 18:26; 28:9,17; Mr 1:40; 5:6,7; Lu 5:12 Joh 9:38; 1Co 14:25; Re 19:10; 22:8,9 if. 9:28,29; 13:58; Mr 9:22-24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-3","title":"Matthew 8:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>put. 2Ki 5:11 I will. Ge 1:3; Ps 33:9; Mr 1:41; 4:39; 5:41; 7:34; 9:25; Lu 5:13; 7:14 Joh 5:21; 11:43; 15:24 immediately. 11:4,5; 2Ki 5:14; Lu 17:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-4","title":"Matthew 8:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>See. 6:1; 9:30; 12:16-19; 16:20; 17:9; Mr 1:43,44; 5:43; 7:36; Lu 5:14 Joh 5:41; 7:18; 8:50 shew. 3:15; 5:17; Le 13:2-46; 14:2-32; Isa 42:21; Lu 17:14 for. 10:18; 2Ki 5:7,8; Mr 1:44; 6:11; 13:9; Lu 5:14; 21:13; Joh 10:37,38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-5","title":"Matthew 8:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>entered. 4:13; 9:1; 11:23; Mr 2:1; Lu 7:1 a centurion.This was a Roman military title; and therefore this officer may be concluded to have been a Gentile. (See fuller particulars under Mark 15:39.)</p>\n<p>27:54; Mr 15:39; Lu 7:2-10; Ac 10:1-33; 22:25; 23:17,23; 27:13,31,43</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-6","title":"Matthew 8:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>my. Job 31:13,14; Ac 10:7; Col 3:11; 4:1; 1Ti 6:2; Phm 1:16 palsy. 4:24; 9:2; Mr 2:3-12; Ac 8:7; 9:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-7","title":"Matthew 8:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>I will. 9:18,19; Mr 5:23,24; Lu 7:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-8","title":"Matthew 8:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>I am. 3:11,14; 15:26,27; Ge 32:10; Ps 10:17; Lu 5:8; 7:6,7; 15:19,21 Joh 1:27; 13:6-8 but. 3; Nu 20:8; Ps 33:9; 107:20; Mr 1:25-27; Lu 7:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-9","title":"Matthew 8:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Go. Job 38:34,35; Ps 107:25-29; 119:91; 148:8; Jer 47:6,7; Eze 14:17-21 Mr 4:39-41; Lu 4:35,36,39; 7:8 Do. Eph 6:5,6; Col 3:22; Tit 2:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-10","title":"Matthew 8:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>he marvelled. Mr 6:6; Lu 7:9 I have. 15:28; Lu 5:20; 7:50</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-11","title":"Matthew 8:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>That. 24:31; Ge 12:3; 22:18; 28:14; 49:10; Ps 22:27; 98:3; Isa 2:2,3; 11:10 Isa 49:6; 52:10; 60:1-6; Jer 16:19; Da 2:44; Mic 4:1,2; Zec 8:20-23 Mal 1:11; Lu 13:29; 14:23,24; Ac 10:45; 11:18; 14:27; Ro 15:9-13 Ga 3:28,29; Eph 2:11-14; 3:6; Col 3:11; Re 7:6 shall sit.[Anaklino klino ,] shall recline, i.e., at table; referring to the recumbent posture used by the easterners at their meals.</p>\n<p>Lu 12:37; 13:29; 16:22; Re 3:20,21 in. 3:2; Lu 13:28; Ac 14:22; 1Co 6:9; 15:20; 2Th 1:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-12","title":"Matthew 8:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>the children. 3:9,10; 7:22,23; 21:43; Ac 3:25; Ro 9:4 be cast. 13:42,50; 22:12,13; 24:51; 25:30; Lu 13:28; 2Pe 2:4,17; Jude 1:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-13","title":"Matthew 8:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Go. 4; Ec 9:7; Mr 7:29; Joh 4:50 and as. 9:29,30; 15:28; 17:20; Mr 9:23 And his. Joh 4:52,53</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-14","title":"Matthew 8:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>into. 20; 17:25; Mr 1:29-31; Lu 4:38,39 wife's. 1Co 9:5; 1Ti 3:2; 4:3; Heb 13:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-15","title":"Matthew 8:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>touched. 3; 9:20,29; 14:36; 20:34; 2Ki 13:21; Isa 6:7; Mr 1:41; Lu 8:54 Ac 19:11-13 and ministered. Lu 4:38,39; Joh 12:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-16","title":"Matthew 8:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>the even. Mr 1:32-34; Lu 4:40 they brought. 4:24; 9:2; Mr 2:3; Ac 5:15 and he. 12:22; Mr 1:25-27,34; 5:8; 9:25; Ac 19:13-16 and healed. 14:14; Ex 15:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-17","title":"Matthew 8:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>it might. 1:22; 2:15,23 Himself. Isa 53:4; 1Pe 2:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-18","title":"Matthew 8:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>saw. 1; Mr 1:35-38; Lu 4:42,43; Joh 6:15 unto. 14:22; Mr 4:35; 5:21; 6:45; 8:13; Lu 8:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-19","title":"Matthew 8:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>certain. Ezr 7:6; Mr 12:32-34; Lu 9:57,58; 1Co 1:20 I will. Lu 14:25-27,33; 22:33,34; Joh 13:36-38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-20","title":"Matthew 8:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>and. Ps 84:3; 104:17 the Son. Ps 40:17; 69:29; 109:22; Isa 53:2,3; Lu 2:7,12,16; 8:3; 2Co 8:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-21","title":"Matthew 8:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>another. Lu 9:59-62 suffer. 19:29; Le 21:11,12; Nu 6:6,7; De 33:9,10; 1Ki 19:20,21; Hag 1:2 2Co 5:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-22","title":"Matthew 8:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>follow. 4:18-22; 9:9; Joh 1:43 and. Lu 15:32; Eph 2:1,5; 5:14; Col 2:13; 1Ti 5:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-23","title":"Matthew 8:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>9:1; Mr 4:36; Lu 7:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-24","title":"Matthew 8:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>there. Ps 107:23-27; Isa 54:11; Jon 1:4,5; Mr 4:37,38; Ac 27:14-38 2Co 11:25,26 but. Lu 8:23; Joh 6:17,18; 11:5,6,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-25","title":"Matthew 8:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>and awoke. Ps 10:1; 44:22,23; Isa 51:9,10; Mr 4:38,39; Lu 8:24 save. 2Ch 14:11; 20:12; Jon 1:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-26","title":"Matthew 8:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Why. 6:30; 14:30,31; 16:8; Isa 41:10-14; Mr 4:40; Lu 8:25; Ro 4:20 and rebuked. 27; Job 38:8-11; Ps 65:7; 89:9; 93:3,4; 104:6-9; 107:28-30; 114:3-7 Pr 8:28,29; Isa 50:2-4; 63:12; Na 1:4; Hab 3:8; Mr 4:39,41; 6:48-51 Lu 8:24,25; Re 10:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-27","title":"Matthew 8:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>14:33; 15:31; Mr 1:27; 6:51; 7:37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-28","title":"Matthew 8:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>when. Mr 5:1-20; Lu 8:26-39; Ac 10:38 Gergesenes.Some are of opinion that Gergasa was the country of the ancient Girgashites; but it is more probable the Gergesenes was introduced by Origen upon mere conjecture; as before him most copies seem to have read Gadarenes, agreeable to the Parallel Passages and the ancient Syriac version. Gadara, says Josephus, was the metropolis of Peraea, or the region beyond Jordan; and he also observes that it was sixty furlongs, or about eight miles from Tiberias. It is therefore rightly placed opposite Tiberias, at the southeast end of the lake. Pliny says it was called Hippodion, was one of the cities of Decapolis, and had the river Hieromax, or Jarmouk, flowing before it. It was of heathen jurisdiction; whence perhaps it was destroyed by the Jews; but was rebuilt by Pompey, and joined to the province of Syria. Augustus afterwards gave it to Herod, on whose death it was again annexed to Syria. It is now called Om Keis; its ruins are in a very mutilated state, and when visited by Burckhardt it had not a single inhabitant. The remains of the sepulchral caverns in which the demoniacs abode are still to be seen.</p>\n<p>Ge 10:16; 15:21; De 7:1 coming. Mr 5:2-5; Lu 8:27,29 so. Jud 5:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-29","title":"Matthew 8:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>What. 2Sa 16:10; 19:22; Joe 3:4; Mr 1:24; 5:7; Lu 4:34; 8:28; Joh 2:4 thou Son. 4:3; Mr 3:11; Lu 4:41; Ac 16:17; Jas 2:19 torment. 2Pe 2:4; Jude 1:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-30","title":"Matthew 8:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>an. Le 11:7; De 14:8; Isa 65:3,4; 66:3; Mr 5:11; Lu 8:32; 15:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-31","title":"Matthew 8:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>Mr 5:7,12; Lu 8:30-33; Re 12:12; 20:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-32","title":"Matthew 8:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>Go. 1Ki 22:22; Job 1:10-12; 2:3-6; Ac 2:23; 4:28; Re 20:7 the whole. Job 1:13-19; 2:7,8; Mr 5:13; Lu 8:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-33","title":"Matthew 8:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>Mr 5:14-16; Lu 8:34-36; Ac 19:15-17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-8-34","title":"Matthew 8:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>they besought. 29; De 5:25; 1Sa 16:4; 1Ki 17:18; 18:17; Job 21:14; 22:17 Mr 5:17,18; Lu 5:8; 8:28,37-39; Ac 16:39</p>"}]}